# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. GitHub cosmetics
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep vendored placeholder art out of the language statistics and out of
# "Files changed" by default. Cosmetic only — has no effect on git itself.
Assets/_Placeholders/** linguist-vendored
*.meta                 linguist-generated


# ==============================================================================
# 6. Git LFS — DISABLED. Read before enabling.
# ==============================================================================
# This repo is ~1.3 GB with 571 PNGs, 255 FBXs and single files up to 59 MB, all
# stored as ordinary git objects. LFS is the right long-term answer, but turning
# it on is a TEAM decision, not a file edit. Before uncommenting:
#
#   1. Every contributor runs `git lfs install` once. If someone commits a
#      matching file without it, they push the raw blob while this file claims
#      it is a pointer — a confusing mixed state.
#   2. Understand that this only affects files committed FROM THAT POINT ON.
#      The existing 1.3 GB stays in history. Shrinking that needs
#      `git lfs migrate import`, which REWRITES HISTORY — every branch, every
#      teammate re-clones. Do not attempt that with branches in flight.
#   3. With no [lfs "<url>"] section in .git/config, LFS resolves its endpoint
#      from `origin` automatically. That is what you want — don't pin one by
#      hand unless you deliberately move hosts.
#
# Suggested timing: after the M0 demo ships, before the artists' real assets
# start landing. Placeholder art is already committed; production art is not.
#
# *.fbx  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.tga  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.psd  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.tif  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.exr  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.hdr  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.wav  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.mp3  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.ogg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.mov  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text


# ==============================================================================
# 7. UnityYAMLMerge setup (each developer, once)
# ==============================================================================
# The merge=unityyamlmerge rules above do nothing until this is configured
# locally. Run once per machine, adjusting the path to your Unity install:
#
#   git config --global merge.unityyamlmerge.name "Unity SmartMerge"
#   git config --global merge.unityyamlmerge.driver \
#     '/path/to/Unity/Editor/Data/Tools/UnityYAMLMerge merge -p %O %A %B %A'
#   git config --global merge.unityyamlmerge.recursive binary
#
# Linux default:   ~/Unity/Hub/Editor/6000.3.12f1/Editor/Data/Tools/UnityYAMLMerge
# Windows default: C:\Program Files\Unity\Hub\Editor\6000.3.12f1\Editor\Data\Tools\UnityYAMLMerge.exe
#
# Without it, git falls back to its normal text merge. Nothing breaks; scene and
# prefab conflicts are just uglier to resolve by hand.
# ==============================================================================
